# AfterCore — Apache / cPanel error documents.
#
# These lines tell an Apache host which static page to serve for each HTTP status. They make
# 400.html, 401.html, 403.html, 404.html, 500.html and 503.html actually appear.
#
# nginx, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, GitHub Pages and most CDNs ignore this file: use
#   - Netlify:            add a _redirects file with "/* /404.html 404"
#   - Cloudflare Pages:   Settings > Custom error pages, point each status at the file below
#   - GitHub Pages:       only 404.html is served automatically
# Delete this file if the host is not Apache, or if it conflicts with the panel's own settings.

ErrorDocument 400 /400.html
ErrorDocument 401 /401.html
ErrorDocument 403 /403.html
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
ErrorDocument 500 /500.html
ErrorDocument 503 /503.html
